  "baseline": "Unmodified Phase8/27 atomic-sentence-rank over same original source sentences and frozen pretrained MS MARCO MiniLM scores.",
  "treatment": "Exact frozen Phase28 semantic-joint-citations: same top-24-plus-best-per-source candidate policy; Qwen selects 2-3 original source sentence IDs from at least two source paragraphs; identical fallback on invalid/abstain/over-cap; fill remainder by same frozen relevance rank.",
  "selector_prompt_system": "You are an evidence-only multi-hop Wikipedia citation verifier. Given a question and numbered verbatim SOURCE sentences from source articles, identify TWO or THREE distinct sentence IDs that together justify the intermediate entity and the TARGET answer relation in the question. At least TWO DIFFERENT Wikipedia source articles MUST contribute sentences. Do NOT rely on world knowledge, inferred titles alone or unquoted facts. If the listed sources do not jointly justify both hops, ABSTAIN. Return one valid JSON object ONLY with keys 'citation_ids' (array of 2 or 3 sentence IDs, or [] on abstention) and 'intermediate_relation' (at most 20 words summarizing the grounded cross-source hop). DO NOT output the target answer as an extra unsupported claim; use exactly the provided candidate sentence IDs, no hallucinated identifiers.",
  "selector_prompt_user_template": "Multi-hop question: {question}\n\nOriginal source sentences:\n{sentences}\n\nOutput grounded citation_ids JSON, [] if two-hop relation cannot be verified.",
  "selector_system_sha256": "195a1eca396ef6ee276113f87a836e70b83418c528244e344ed4cedc67e7cf8b",
  "selector_user_template_sha256": "ac373e5e5c193e3cfe6fb7f918e44a85a85c670070a7cd06bf20606d30f31352",
  "reader": "Same frozen Phase7 short-answer Qwen27B payload, temperature 0, identical prompt on both arms.",
  "model": "qwen3.8-27b-orcarouter-q4km",
  "reranker": "cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2",
  "reranker_revision": "233902d25c440f23af6f7d6e94d2946bac0bee0a",
